/trials
.DS_Store
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.vscode/
manifest.py
# the firmware build recipe's board manifests must be tracked
!firmware/**/manifest.py

# serial capture logs from hardware runs (debug artifacts, not part of the example)
examples/**/*.log

# Provisioning material and per-node state. provision_control_root.py writes the fleet's
# signing half into examples/, and a node writes its identity and replay mark beside it; none
# of it belongs in a published repo, and the signing half is the fleet's whole control plane.
**/control_root.key
**/identity.key
**/control.counter

# The wizard's fleet directory (tools/provision.py, default ./allora-fleet). Its backups hold a
# board's identity scalar under its own name, which the bare `identity.key` pattern above does
# not match, and a fleet is one operator's deployment state rather than anything this library
# ships. The whole directory stays out.
allora-fleet/
**/*.identity.key

# CI firmware artifacts downloaded for a bench session (`gh run download`). Re-downloadable
# from the workflow run the session's notes cite, so they are not history, and each is close
# to two megabytes.
firmware/_dl_*/
